      "content": "Each claim carries one evidence label: implemented | read directly from code at the pinned commit configured | a default, environment variable, packaging or launcher setting tested | exercised by a test in the Lear repository (and, where stated, run on 2026-11-05) inferred | a conclusion drawn from reading the code; no single line proves it Evidence is written `path:Lstart-Lend`, relative to the Lear repository root, at commit `60cf9abf8408`. `python -m ragformation lear docs verify --source <checkout>` re-checks every reference against that commit. [2] Evidence: `prash/permissions.py:L37-L64`. - [implemented] The circuit breaker opens for a resource after `max_actions` executions inside `window_seconds` and keeps its state in a JSON file so the cap survives restarts. [1]",
