      "content": "Each claim carries one evidence label: implemented | read directly from code at the pinned commit configured | a default, environment variable, packaging or launcher setting tested | exercised by a test in the Lear repository (and, where stated, run on 2026-11-05) inferred | a conclusion drawn from reading the code; no single line proves it Evidence is written `path:Lstart-Lend`, relative to the Lear repository root, at commit `60cf9abf8408`. `python -m ragformation lear docs verify --source <checkout>` re-checks every reference against that commit. [1] Evidence: `prash/audit.py:L67-L80`. - [inferred] Because the sequence is read and then appended without a lock, two processes appending at the same moment can write the same `seq`; the log stays append-only but the sequence is not guaranteed unique under concurrency. - [implemented] The circuit-breaker state is written with a plain `write_text` (no temporary file and rename). [5] Evidence: `prash/permissions.py:L37-L64`. - [implemented] The circuit breaker opens for a resource after `max_actions` executions inside `window_seconds` and keeps its state in a JSON file so the cap survives restarts. [3]",
