    {
      "message_id": 36,
      "session_id": "rec-s07-20261106T1219Z",
      "user_id": "rec-u07",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Evidence: `prash/server.py:L2641-L2700`. - [implemented] For the duration of that call the handler swaps `cli.CliAsk` for an ask object that always answers yes, so prompts raised by the permission engine are approved automatically. [1] Evidence: `prash/cli.py:L1254`, `prash/cli.py:L277`. - [implemented] A dry run consults the permission engine but never calls `execute`; a refusal is reported as refused instead of showing a plan. [3]",
